extraction_notes: "WB9 South America 2 printed 107-109 (cache p107-p109, page_offset 0); lore 107-108, abilities 108-109, the O.C.C. block on 109. Printed 108 and 109 checked against a 200 dpi render; the OCR agreed on every number (the OCR reads [AR-20 for IAR-20). No destroyer-borg class was in production on 2026-09-25. || XP: the Destroyer ''Borg and Inca Warrior ladder on printed 192, read off a render; the level 10 figure prints 98.001 with a period and is stored as 98001. || GROUP: the book files the O.C.C. under the Megaversal Legion, not under a group heading; stored as men-of-arms (a combat cyborg). mdc_base is stated, so no men_of_arms line. || BODY: mdc_base holds the main body, 300; the limbs, hands, feet and the 100 M.D.C. spinal column are in the Full Bionic Reconstruction ability. The 150 M.D.C. force field is a per-activation barrier with three charges and is prose, not a pool. || ATTRIBUTES: the book grants robotic P.S. 35 and P.P. 26, stored as fixed attribute_dice. Mental attributes and P.B. are the character''s own and are left to the defaults. Speed is printed only as 70 mph (112 km/h), with no Spd number, so no Spd is stored and the speed is in the ability. The ''borg is not flagged supersedes_race: the book opens it to ''human or humanoid'' troopers, the brain and its knowledge are the character''s own, and a humanoid race''s pools and dice therefore win a pairing as they do for every other cyborg O.C.C. here. Played as a human (no R.C.C.), everything applies as printed. || BONUSES: printed 109 gives COMBINED totals that include attribute bonuses: +1 attack, +3 initiative, +4 strike, +1 strike with ranged weapons, +6 parry, +8 dodge, +3 pull punch, +3 save vs horror factor. The sheet adds the P.P. 26 chart (+6 strike, parry and dodge) by itself, so what is stored is each total less that share: strike -2, parry 0 (omitted), dodge +2; attacks, initiative, pull punch and horror factor are stored whole because no attribute feeds them. The sheet therefore shows the printed totals. The ranged-only +1 strike is conditional and is an ability. Robot P.S. damage is the book''s table, in the ability. || SKILLS: American (98%) as Language: Native Tongue 98, following the Mining ''Borg; Dakir Common (98%) as a Language: Other pick fixed at 98 (no Dakir row, none stubbed); two languages +15 as two Language: Other picks. Basic and Advanced Math +15 as Mathematics: Basic and Mathematics: Advanced at 60. Basic Radio 45+15; Detect Ambush 30+10; Pilot: Tank and APC (hover) +15 as Military: Tanks & APCs 36+15; Sniper; Wilderness Survival 30+10; Prowl 25+15, plus the +5% the stealth systems add, stored as 45. W.P. Assault Rifle is the catalog''s W.P. Automatic and Semi-automatic Rifles. Hand to Hand: Expert changes to Martial Arts or Assassin for one other skill; no alignment condition is printed. || RELATED: seven, plus two at levels 3 and 5 and one at 8, 10 and 12. Bonuses as printed: Communications +10, Espionage +8, Medical (Paramedic only) +5, Military +10, Pilot +10, Rogue +5, Science +5, Technical +10, Wilderness +5; Domestic, Electrical, Mechanical, Physical, Pilot Related and W.P. any. Secondary: five, same limits without the bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: the ARP-1 or IAR-20 as a choice; one energy weapon of choice from a catalog set; four E-clips; survival knife; first-aid kit. The book gives four E-clips or magazines for EACH weapon, so the rifle''s four more (E-clips for the ARP-1, magazines for the IAR-20) are recorded here, not stored. The field kit has no catalog row and is not stubbed. || MONEY: pay is 3000 credits a month plus room, board, bionics and equipment, with 1000 more a month hazard pay in combat; the character starts with one month''s pay, stored as 3000. || CYBERNETICS: the book says ''see above''; the bionic systems are the abilities."
---

## Lore

The Destroyer ''Borgs are human or humanoid legionnaires rebuilt into total bionic
conversions, in effect robots carrying a living brain. The Dakir designed them
for small-unit work: squads of twelve split into three-man teams that scout,
make surgical strikes and run long missions far from support. Because the
bodies need neither food nor water and power their own weapons, a team can sit
in ambush for months, slip behind enemy lines to wear down defences before an
attack, or hunt foes through the jungle.

The Dakir alloys are decades ahead of anything Triax builds, so the frame is
both lighter and tougher than a normal cyborg''s. It is nearly skeletal, the
upper body joined to the legs by little more than a metal spine, which makes
it fast and quiet. Heads are sculpted to taste, and many Destroyers choose
monstrous faces to frighten the enemy. Each one also carries a built-in
virtual-reality system, a refuge from the grim life of a machine soldier.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'destroyer-borg');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'destroyer-borg';

